  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nHigh pressure that is over the region today will push eastward\ntonight. An upper level trough will move into the Upper Great\nLakes region on Wednesday. A cold front will push through the\nGreat Lakes and into the Upper Ohio Valley late Wednesday.\nSurface dewpoints will climb into the lower 70s by Wednesday\nafternoon. High temperatures will reach the middle to upper 80s\non Wednesday. 0-6km shear will increase to 40 to 45 knots and modest\ninstability will develop of 1000-2000 J/kg ahead of the cold \nfront late Wednesday. There is a marginal risk for severe\nstorms ahead of the cold front with the main threat being\nisolated damaging wind gusts. PW values will increase to around\n2 inches which will support heavy downpours and localized heavy\nrainfall possible. The time window for possible severe weather\nwill be between 4 pm and 10 pm. The cold front will slow down\nas it moves into central Ohio Wednesday night. Another weak area\nof low pressure will ride along the frontal boundary late\nWednesday night into Thursday with another round of rain likely,\nespecially for areas south of Highway 30. The front and rain\nchances will finally clear out of the area by Thursday evening.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nHigh pressure will build in over the Great Lakes and the Upper\nOhio Valley Friday and Saturday. High temperatures will be in\nthe middle to upper 70s on Friday and lower to middle 80s by\nSaturday. A weak cold front will try to move through the Great\nLakes region late Sunday but stall out just north of our area.\nWarm and humid weather will continue into early next week.",
